+`identity-registry.json` contains 66 manually reviewed public fictional-identity records, with canonical names, deliberately limited aliases, franchise context, source URLs, review date and factual decision basis. `build-ai-read.cjs` embeds this data into the existing eligibility module. There is no runtime network dependency or registry writer.
+
+Publisher biographies are preferred. Explicit encyclopedic character classifications corroborate established identities where publisher evidence is limited. These are reviewed factual assertions, not copied biographies, images, scraped databases, appearance inference or pronoun-only inference. URLs are attribution/provenance, not instructions. Existing MIT code licensing is unchanged; source publications and character rights retain their respective ownership. Future changes require another source review and regression tests; source availability and references may change.
+
+An eligibility record does not assert scene presence. The existing filename/title association, ignored-tag, taxonomy-conflict, duplicate-native-alias, fresh-state and additive-only gates are unchanged. In particular, multiple native Tags for Lili/Emilie De Rochefort or Sue/Susan Storm remain blocked even though the canonical identities are documented. No tag merge, rename, removal, ignore-preference change or metadata repair is performed.
+
+Read results add `evidenceSources` and `registryRevision` when available. Existing policy/API version 1 and legacy `character_identity_v1` semantics remain unchanged. Classification uncertainty is not a metadata deletion recommendation. Names not corroborated sufficiently remain unresolved, including short/shared labels and gender ambiguity; this does not prove those identities are ineligible. Real performer verification is not expanded.
+
